an a sharp capitulation, and it lends the bearish structure a degree of conviction that erratic moves rarely produce.\n\nThe structure story begins at the prior reaction zone around 1.6501, a level that attracted sellers on multiple occasions through early July and capped each attempted recovery. Price has since traded well below that ceiling, and the zone now sits as overhead resistance some 200 pips distant. Closer overhead, the 1.6340 area \u2014 another prior reaction zone with three touches \u2014 has been tested and rejected in recent sessions, with the 22nd and 23rd of July both printing highs in that vicinity before sellers reasserted themselves. That level is the more immediate reference point for any intraday recovery attempt. To the downside, the next meaningful structural reference sits at the 1.6204 prior reaction zone, with a secondary cluster just beneath at 1.6189. Those two levels represent the next logical area where demand could materialise should the current drift continue.\n\nThe H1 picture over the past 24 hours shows a pair that is largely directionless on the shorter timeframe, oscillating in a roughly 70-pip band between 1.6236 and 1.6315. The early European session produced a brief spike lower toward 1.6236 during the 05:00\u201307:00 window before recovering, suggesting that the lower end of this consolidation has attracted some intraday interest. Since then, price has drifted back toward the upper portion of the range, hovering just below 1.6300. The H1 structure reads as a compression zone beneath the 1.6340 resistance, consistent with a pause within the broader downtrend rather than a base-building reversal.\n\nToday's economic calendar carries no scheduled high-impact events for either the euro or the Australian dollar, which points toward a session likely dominated by positioning and technical flows rather than fundamental catalysts. The absence of data removes the prospect of sharp directional breaks driven by news, but it also means any drift lower would lack the momentum that a catalyst typically provides.\n\nThe bearish read would come under pressure if price were to reclaim and close above the 1.6340 prior reaction zone on the daily chart, as that would break the sequence of lower highs that has defined the July trend. A sustained move back toward 1.6500 would materially alter the structural picture. Until that occurs, the path of least resistance appears to remain to the downside, with the 1.6204 support zone as the next area of interest.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}